CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pack of 2 deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ pack of 3 deduced: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ wrong value FAILs \(non-vacuous\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.spec.partial.match] / [temp.class.spec]: a class template partial
specialization whose pattern is a template-id with a pack expansion
(primary<Types...>) must match a concrete instantiation, deducing the pack.
CBMC matched the nested template-id arguments positionally and never deduced the
pack, so the partial specialization was never selected (the incomplete primary
template was used and the member accesses were silently dropped).  This is the
shape of std::tuple_size<std::tuple<Types...>> and many variadic traits.
Assertions 1 and 2 prove the pack of 2 / 3 is deduced; assertion 3 (a wrong
value) is expected to FAIL, proving the deduced value is genuinely checked
(non-vacuous).  (A zero-length pack -- primary<> / std::tuple<> -- is a separate
sub-case that does not yet resolve.)
